{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines the Transition as US securities moving from T+2 to T+1 effective 28 May 2024 and explains compressed post-trade timing and Hong Kong time-zone impact.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0"},{"reason":"Addresses SFC reminder to LCs to assess impact and take appropriate operational, technology, systems and staffing measures.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498"},{"reason":"States that LCs should assess readiness and ability to cope with the shortened cycle.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879"},{"reason":"Specifies liquidity-risk review, funding availability, cross-currency mismatch and settlement-failure concerns, including FX remaining T+2.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"},{"reason":"Addresses staff availability, optional shift or hours arrangements, automation, and required training for timely settlement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"reason":"Addresses proactive client engagement and communication for potentially affected clients.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916"},{"reason":"Introduces separate reminders for management companies of SFC-authorised funds, especially those with considerable US-securities exposure.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116"},{"reason":"Requires fund impact assessment concerning subscription money or sale proceeds from non-US markets used to purchase US securities.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u7.2267"},{"reason":"Addresses fund arrangements such as pre-funding and additional staff where necessary, with fair, orderly and investor-interest objectives.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u8.2499"},{"reason":"Addresses early alerts by fund managers to SFC and investors and remedial action for material effects.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u9.2771"},{"reason":"States continuing SFC monitoring of market developments.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u10.2996"},{"reason":"Identifies issuing SFC divisions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u11.3083"},{"reason":"Identifies Intermediaries Division and SFC.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u12.3172"},{"reason":"Identifies the Securities and Futures Commission.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u13.3290"},{"reason":"Footnote examples define US securities to include equities, bonds, exchange-traded funds and options.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336"},{"reason":"Canada footnote states Canada transitions to T+1 on 27 May 2024 and that Transition includes US and Canada.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"},{"reason":"Defines post-trade settlement processes as including trade allocation, confirmation and affirmation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The operative LC language applies to licensed corporations. A distinct later section applies to management companies of SFC-authorised funds, particularly those with considerable US-securities exposures; that fund section should not automatically be imposed on an LC unless it also acts in that capacity.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Transition means US and Canadian securities settlement moving to T+1 (US effective 28 May 2024; Canada 27 May 2024). US securities examples are equities, bonds, ETFs and options. Post-trade processes include trade allocation, confirmation and affirmation.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Staff shift changes, extended hours, evening or morning duties, automation, expanded pre-funding and additional staff are framed as possible or conditional measures. The Canada footnote extends the defined Transition geographically; it does not create an exception to LC duties. The phrase 'where appropriate' and 'where necessary' leaves implementation choice open.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u8.2499","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The circular uses 'wishes to remind', 'should assess', 'should be mindful', and 'should' for LC readiness, liquidity, funding, staffing, training and client engagement. 'May consider' marks optional examples rather than mandatory adoption of each measure. The text does not expressly state a sanction or an absolute requirement to adopt every listed measure.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The Transition dates are 27 May 2024 for Canada and 28 May 2024 for the US. The readiness and operational consequences concern operations after the Transition. FX remains T+2, creating a continuing cycle mismatch for cross-currency transactions.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Readiness depends on the shortened US/Canada securities cycle, the unchanged FX T+2 cycle for cross-currency transactions, Hong Kong time-zone differences, and the defined post-trade processes. Fund-specific duties depend on fund exposure and use of non-US subscription money or sale proceeds.","source_unit_ids":["d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u7.2267","d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"],"status":"PROPOSED"}],"questions":["Does 'should' in this SFC reminder represent a supervisory expectation requiring documented implementation, or guida